<urn:atm:triage:finding/AXPE-FLAKY-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AXPE-FLAKY-002" ;
  triage:title "Busy-spin polling loops gated by a fixed 1s wall-clock timeout instead of a notification primitive" ;
  triage:description "cancel_inflight_prompt() (~:1700 and ~:1715) and ac11_successful_prompt_cancellation_cannot_rerelease_claim (~:3228) spin `loop { ...; tokio::task::yield_now().await }` on fake.calls() / list_pending_members() inside tokio::time::timeout(1s). The 1s ceiling doubles as the pass/fail bound on a spawn_blocking-backed completion; under CI contention the spin competes with the blocking pool it waits on. The same file already has the Notify-based install_handoff_cleanup_test_gate/await_handoff_cleanup_test_gate seam. Remediation: signal completion with a Notify/oneshot fired after the blocking work (test-only seam like the existing gate), await it, and keep the timeout only as an outer hang diagnostic. Watch RULE-003: herdr_queue_wake.rs is at 997/1000 production lines per .just/check_line_counts.py, so any production-side seam must land in a sibling module." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "phase_end_review" ;
  triage:category "flaky-test-qa" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "phase" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-06T00:20:56Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
